# What the application package ships, and where.
#
# EVERYTHING GOES UNDER /opt/tt-bio-demo, not into dist-packages. These are
# not libraries anyone should import: `ui` and `runner` are two halves of one
# application that run under two DIFFERENT interpreters (venv-ui has GTK and
# no torch; venv-runner has torch/ttnn and no GTK -- see the project's
# CLAUDE.md), and `protocol` is deliberately importable by both. Installing
# `ui/` or `protocol/` into the system Python would put three top-level names
# that generic on every Python path on the machine.
#
# Listed directory by directory rather than as a glob of the repo root. A
# glob would ship tests/, .venvs/, generated/, recordings/ and the docs tree
# the first time someone added one -- and a package that quietly grows is one
# nobody notices growing. `test_tests_and_scratch_do_not_ship` is what holds
# this line.

ui                  opt/tt-bio-demo/
runner              opt/tt-bio-demo/
protocol            opt/tt-bio-demo/
playlist            opt/tt-bio-demo/
examples            opt/tt-bio-demo/
scripts             opt/tt-bio-demo/
VERSION             opt/tt-bio-demo/
